IMPORT prelude

-- EXPECTED RED for row IL-34 (added 2026-11-09): a FINDING ABOUT THE REGULATION, not about the Law and not about this
-- encoding. Exactly 4 assertions here are expected to fail; check.sh's `expected_failed` table and encoding.json's
-- `expected_red` both carry that count. None of them changes an answer the rules give: this row takes the full rate and
-- the threshold as inputs (nii-s342e-several-employers.l4, NOTES.md section 3), so the regulation's stale words gate nothing.
--
-- THE FINDING. The National Insurance (Payment and Deduction of Insurance Contributions from the Pay of an Insured
-- Person Working for Different Employers) Regulations, 5757-1997, were never conformed to the Law they exercise.
-- Reg 1 defines "the full rate" by "column E of Schedule J, on the part of the wage above half the average wage", and reg 2
-- says "not above half the average wage, as stated in s 342(e)(3) of the Law".
-- Since 1 January 2006 the Law's own s 342(e)(3) says column D (the employee's deduction column) and "60% of the average wage",
-- and since 1 January 2026 "the reduced collection threshold". So the regulation names a column that is now the Treasury's
-- allocation, and a threshold that the Law has twice moved from. It was RIGHT when made (the first three passing
-- assertions): in 1997 the employee's deduction was column E of Schedule J, and s 342(e)(3) as added that year said column E and
-- half the average wage.
-- In practice a court would read reg 1's column as the employee-deduction column; the finding is about the text, severity low.
--
-- WHAT WAS READ, AND WHAT WAS NOT. The regulation's text (regs 1 and 2 as made) and the Law's text were each read from page
-- images of the official instruments, not only from the Wikisource consolidations:
--   reg 1 and reg 2 as made: Kovetz HaTakanot 5835, 17.6.1997, p. 864 (registers/source-bundle/regulations/takanot-5835-orig-5757-p864.pdf,
--     PDF page 8). That PDF is a scan of the Reshumot issue hosted by olaw.org.il, a private archive, not the Government Printer's copy.
--   s 342(e)(3)-(4) as added: Sefer HaChukim 1607, 7.1.1997, pp. 36-37 (amending-laws/14_lsr_211373.pdf, PDF pages 21-22);
--   as replaced: Sefer HaChukim 2023, 10.8.2005, p. 809, s 66(3)(a) (16_lsr_299994.pdf, PDF page 45), in force from 1.1.2006 by
--     s 80(a) and (k) (pp. 819, 824); and the threshold words as replaced: Sefer HaChukim 3384, 27.3.2025, pp. 395-396, s 19(4) and
--     s 21 (25_lsr_6133485.pdf, PDF pages 11-12), in force from 1.1.2026;
--   Schedule J as enacted: Sefer HaChukim 1522, 15.5.1995, p. 302 (13_lsr_203774.pdf, PDF page 93), column E headed the deduction
--     from the employee's wage for s 342(c).
-- NOT checked: the Kovetz HaTakanot indexes after 1999. The amendments of the regulations that the consolidation lists
-- (Kovetz HaTakanot 5848 p. 1112, 5905 p. 892, 5956 p. 440) were read where they touch regs 1 and 2 and none changes the column
-- letter or the threshold; a later amendment of reg 1 or reg 2, if there is one, would void this finding and is not ruled out.
-- The Hebrew on the `ext:` lines below is transcribed from the page images by hand and is not checked mechanically against a
-- source file (the tag names the page); the `ext:[reg-several]` line is the mechanically expanded consolidation line.

§ `Tests expected to fail: the regulation of 5757-1997 against the Law as it now stands`

§§ `What each instrument names`

-- reg 1 and reg 2 as made, Kovetz HaTakanot 5835 p. 864 (transcribed from the page image):
-- ext:[KT5835-p864] | ״שיעור מלא״ – שיעור הניכוי משכר העובד הקבוע בטור ה׳ בלוח י׳ לחוק, על חלק השכר העולה על מחצית השכר הממוצע;
-- ext:[KT5835-p864] | מעביד שתקנות 5(א) ו־(ה)(1) לתקנות הניכוי חלות לגביו, ינכה דמי ביטוח בשיעור מלא גם מחלק השכר של העובד, שאינו עולה על מחצית השכר הממוצע, כאמור בסעיף 342(ה)(3) לחוק.
-- the same two words in the regulation's consolidation, which has them unchanged (reg 2 there also names the "recognised employer"):
-- ext:[reg-several] 18 | ”שיעור מלא“ – שיעור הניכוי משכר העובד הקבוע בטור ה׳ בלוח י׳ לחוק, על חלק השכר העולה על מחצית השכר הממוצע;
-- s 342(e)(3) as added in 1997, Sefer HaChukim 1607 p. 36 (transcribed from the page image):
-- ext:[SH1607-p36] | (3) חובת מעביד לנכות דמי ביטוח בשיעור החל, לפי טור ה׳ בלוח י׳, על הכנסת עובד העולה על מחצית השכר הממוצע, גם מהכנסת העובד שאינה עולה על מחצית השכר הממוצע, אם העובד מועסק אצל מעביד נוסף;
-- s 342(e)(3) as replaced from 1.1.2006, Sefer HaChukim 2023 p. 809, s 66(3)(a)(1) (transcribed from the page image):
-- ext:[SH2023-p809] | ״(3) חובת מעביד לנכות דמי ביטוח בשיעור החל, לפי טור ד׳ בלוח י׳, על הכנסת עובד העולה על 60% מהשכר הממוצע, גם מהכנסת העובד שאינה עולה על 60% מהשכר הממוצע, אם העובד מועסק אצל מעביד נוסף;״
-- the words of s 342, as replaced from 1.1.2026, Sefer HaChukim 3384 p. 396, s 19(4) (transcribed from the page image):
-- ext:[SH3384-p396] | בסעיף 342, בכל מקום, במקום ״60% מהשכר הממוצע״ יבוא ״מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת״, ובמקום ״מ־60% מהשכר הממוצע״ יבוא ״ממדרגת הגבייה המופחתת״;
-- Schedule J as enacted, Sefer HaChukim 1522 p. 302, the header of column E (transcribed from the rotated page image):
-- ext:[SH1522-p302] | טור ה׳ | הניכוי משכר העובד לענין סעיף 342(ג)

DECLARE `A column letter of Schedule J` IS ONE OF
    `letter A`
    `letter B`
    `letter C`
    `letter D`
    `letter E`

DECLARE `A threshold for the full rate` IS ONE OF
    `threshold: half the average wage`
    `threshold: 60% of the average wage`
    `threshold: the reduced collection threshold`

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 1, "full rate" (Kovetz HaTakanot 5835 p. 864; reg line 18)
GIVETH A `A column letter of Schedule J`
`the column of Schedule J that reg 1 of 5757-1997 names for the full rate` MEANS `letter E`

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 1, "full rate" (Kovetz HaTakanot 5835 p. 864; reg line 18)
GIVETH A `A threshold for the full rate`
`the threshold that reg 1 of 5757-1997 names for the full rate` MEANS `threshold: half the average wage`

@ref Regulations of 5757-1997 reg 2 (Kovetz HaTakanot 5835 p. 864; reg line 23)
GIVETH A `A threshold for the full rate`
`the threshold that reg 2 of 5757-1997 names` MEANS `threshold: half the average wage`

@ref Schedule J as enacted (Sefer HaChukim 1522 p. 302), column E
GIVETH A `A column letter of Schedule J`
`the column of Schedule J headed the deduction from the employee's wage, as enacted in 1995` MEANS `letter E`

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(e)(3) as added (Sefer HaChukim 1607 p. 36)
GIVETH A `A column letter of Schedule J`
`the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(3) named when the regulations were made` MEANS `letter E`

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(e)(3) as added (Sefer HaChukim 1607 p. 36)
GIVETH A `A threshold for the full rate`
`the threshold that s 342(e)(3) named when the regulations were made` MEANS `threshold: half the average wage`

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(e)(3) as replaced (Sefer HaChukim 2023 p. 809, s 66(3)(a)(1); in force from 1 January 2006, s 80(a) and (k))
GIVETH A `A column letter of Schedule J`
`the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(3) has named since 1 January 2006` MEANS `letter D`

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(e)(3) as replaced (Sefer HaChukim 2023 p. 809, s 66(3)(a)(1); in force from 1 January 2006, s 80(a) and (k))
GIVETH A `A threshold for the full rate`
`the threshold that s 342(e)(3) named from 1 January 2006 to 31 December 2025` MEANS `threshold: 60% of the average wage`

@ref National Insurance Law s 342 as amended (Sefer HaChukim 3384 p. 396, s 19(4); in force from 1 January 2026, s 21)
GIVETH A `A threshold for the full rate`
`the threshold that s 342(e)(3) names from 1 January 2026` MEANS `threshold: the reduced collection threshold`

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule J, header, as now printed (source lines 4716-4717 of row IL-04's deposited text)
GIVETH A `A column letter of Schedule J`
`the column of Schedule J headed the deduction from the employee's wage, as now printed` MEANS `letter D`

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule J, header, as now printed (source lines 4716-4717 of row IL-04's deposited text)
GIVETH A `A column letter of Schedule J`
`the column of Schedule J headed the State Treasury's allocation under s 32(c1), as now printed` MEANS `letter E`

§§ `EXPECTED TO FAIL (4): what the regulation names is not what the Law now names`

-- (1) the column: reg 1 says E, the Law says D.
#ASSERT `the column of Schedule J that reg 1 of 5757-1997 names for the full rate` EQUALS `the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(3) has named since 1 January 2006`
-- (2) the threshold in reg 1: half the average wage, where the Law said 60% from 1 January 2006 ...
#ASSERT `the threshold that reg 1 of 5757-1997 names for the full rate` EQUALS `the threshold that s 342(e)(3) named from 1 January 2006 to 31 December 2025`
-- (3) ... and says the reduced collection threshold from 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `the threshold that reg 1 of 5757-1997 names for the full rate` EQUALS `the threshold that s 342(e)(3) names from 1 January 2026`
-- (4) the threshold in reg 2, which cites s 342(e)(3) itself.
#ASSERT `the threshold that reg 2 of 5757-1997 names` EQUALS `the threshold that s 342(e)(3) names from 1 January 2026`

§§ `Checks that pass, to show the comparison can pass and that the failures above are the regulation's drift`

-- When it was made (1997) the regulation named what the Law named, and the column it named was the employee's deduction column.
#ASSERT `the column of Schedule J that reg 1 of 5757-1997 names for the full rate` EQUALS `the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(3) named when the regulations were made`
#ASSERT `the threshold that reg 1 of 5757-1997 names for the full rate` EQUALS `the threshold that s 342(e)(3) named when the regulations were made`
#ASSERT `the column of Schedule J that reg 1 of 5757-1997 names for the full rate` EQUALS `the column of Schedule J headed the deduction from the employee's wage, as enacted in 1995`
-- The Law's s 342(e)(3) now names the deduction column; the column reg 1 names is now the Treasury allocation.
#ASSERT `the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(3) has named since 1 January 2006` EQUALS `the column of Schedule J headed the deduction from the employee's wage, as now printed`
#ASSERT `the column of Schedule J that reg 1 of 5757-1997 names for the full rate` EQUALS `the column of Schedule J headed the State Treasury's allocation under s 32(c1), as now printed`
